                <pb facs="0261" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24472: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Mexicali</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Boyle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexicali</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-08-18"><hi rendition="#italic">August 18,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received August 19—3:42 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Governor Cantu this afternoon, as forecasted, delivered the reins of government
                    over to Luis M. Salazar and thus brought to a termination the state of factional
                    strife threatened in this district.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Boyle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
